1a4fa59d14103897cc70","short_id":"66b81551","created_at":"2025-08-28T20:19:59.000+02:00","parent_ids":["8a60068bf87979aeeb2deae15918a692bc4fbdab"],"title":"Remove `shellcheck` from the dependency tree","message":"Remove `shellcheck` from the dependency tree\n\nAs far as I can tell, `shellcheck` is only used in the [`check` make target](https://gitlab.archlinux.org/archlinux/devtools/-/blob/master/Makefile?ref_type=heads#L194) which neither the `build()` nor the `check()` functions of the PKGBUILD actually calls.\n\nAside from the fact that it doesn't seem necessary, removing `shellcheck` from the dependency tree would make `devtools` way more accessible and straightforward to bootstrap / build for e.g. port efforts as it would drop the requirement on haskell.\n","author_name":"Robin Candau","author_email":"antiz@archlinux.org","authored_date":"2025-08-28T20:12:25.000+02:00","committer_name":"Robin Candau","committer_email":"antiz@archlinux.org","committed_date":"2025-08-28T20:19:59.000+02:00","trailers":{},"extended_trailers":{},"web_url":"https://gitlab.archlinux.org/archlinux/packaging/packages/devtools/-/commit/66b815516013bd5975841a4fa59d14103897cc70"}]